      "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(2x-3)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$",
