      "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+7x-24}{(x+2)(x-1)(x+4)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+2)(x-1)(x+4)$ gives\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+7x-24=A(x-1)(x+4)+B(x+2)(x+4)+C(x+2)(x-1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)^{2}+7(-2)-24 & =A(-2-1)(-2+4) \\\\  & \\,+B(-2+2)(-2+4) \\\\  & \\,+C(-2+2)(-2-1) \\\\ -30 & =A(-6) \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(1)}^{2}+7(1)-24 & =A(1-1)(1+4) \\\\  & \\,+B(1+2)(1+4) \\\\  & \\,+C(1+2)(1-1) \\\\ 2+7-24 & =B(15) \\\\ -15 & =15B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-4,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-4)^{2}+7(-4)-24 & =A(-4-1)(-4+4) \\\\  & \\,+B(-4+2)(-4+4) \\\\  & \\,+C(-4+2)(-4-1) \\\\ 32-28-24 & =C(10) \\\\ -20 & =C(10) \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B+C & =5+(-1)+(-2)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
